    <string name="help_content_eraser">Remove parts of the image like with an eraser.</string>
    <string name="help_content_brush">Use the size slider to set the brush width. The brush buttons let you choose between a hard or soft brush, marker, calligraphy or arrow.</string>
    <string name="help_content_eyedropper">Tap on the image to select a color.</string>
    <string name="help_content_undo">Tap to undo your previous action.</string>
    <string name="help_content_redo">Tap to redo an undone action.</string>
    <string name="help_content_fill">Tap a connected area to fill it. The tolerance slider sets how similar neighbouring colours must be. You can choose up to three colours and create linear, wavy or circular gradients.</string>
    <string name="help_content_replace">Set the brush size from 5 to 50 and paint over the target area. Then tap the source to copy into the marking.</string>
    <string name="replace_tool_source_hint">Tap\nsource</string>
    <string name="help_content_border">Add a colored border outside the image or crop the edge inward.</string>
    <string name="help_content_transform">Adjust size and crop.</string>
    <string name="help_content_perspective">Drag the four corners to the visible area, then tap the checkmark to straighten it.</string>
    <string name="help_content_place">Move, scale or rotate the active layer, then tap the checkmark to place it.</string>
    <string name="help_content_rotate">Rotate or flip the image.</string>
    <string name="help_content_align">Draw a line along a horizontal or vertical edge, then tap the checkmark to straighten the image.</string>
    <string name="help_content_speech_bubble">Choose the speech bubble shape and set the outline width. You can move, rotate and resize it. Drag the small point to position the tail. The checkmark inserts the speech bubble into the image.</string>
    <string name="help_content_shadow">Create a shadow from the active layer.</string>
    <string name="help_content_clipboard">Move and resize the rectangle to cover the area you want to stamp. Tap on copy or cut to select the area. Move it, then tap on paste to stamp.</string>
    <string name="help_content_selection">Select an area on the active layer, then copy, cut or paste it.</string>
    <string name="help_content_import_png">Import an image from the gallery to the clipboard.</string>
    <string name="help_content_line">Draw a straight line.</string>
    <string name="help_content_text">Enter text and choose the font, size, colour and alignment. The buttons below set the outline, shadow and background colour. You can move, rotate, enlarge or reduce the text. A single line can also be curved. The checkmark inserts the text into the image.</string>
    <string name="help_content_shape">Search stickers and insert the selected sticker.</string>
    <string name="help_content_layer">Create new layers or modify existing ones.</string>
    <string name="help_content_color_chooser">Select or adjust a color.</string>
    <string name="help_content_hand">Move your finger to move the canvas.</string>
    <string name="help_content_smudge">Use the size slider to set the smudge area. Drag over the image to smudge colours. The circle appears only while moving.</string>
    <string name="help_content_warp">Use the size slider to set the affected area. Drag over the image to deform the pixels inside the circle. The circle appears only while moving.</string>
    <string name="help_content_pixel">Pixelate the whole image or a selected circular area.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_bilateral">Smooths small uneven areas and image noise without blurring clear edges too much. Use the slider to set the strength of the effect.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_invert">Inverts all colours in the image. Black becomes white and every colour changes to its opposite.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_brightness">Makes all image areas evenly lighter or darker. Bright areas can become white more quickly.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_exposure">Increases or reduces the light already present in the image. This changes the image more naturally.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_contrast">Increases or reduces the difference between light and dark areas. Use the slider to set the contrast.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_blur">Softens the image and blurs details. Use the slider to set the strength.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_bloom">Creates a soft glow around bright areas. Use the slider to set the strength.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_median">Smooths small imperfections and image noise while keeping edges as clear as possible.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_saturation">Use the slider to make colours stronger or weaker. Move left to weaken them until the image is grey, or right to make them stronger.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_hue">Shifts all image colours through the colour spectrum. Use the slider to choose the new hue.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_vibrance">Strengthens mainly weak colours without changing already vivid colours too much. Use the slider to set the strength.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_temperature">Makes the image cooler or warmer. Move left for blue tones and right for yellow or red tones.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_highlights">Changes only the bright parts of the image. Use the slider to make highlights lighter or darker.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_shadows">Changes only the dark parts of the image. Use the slider to make shadows lighter or darker.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_sepia">Gives the image a warm brown sepia look. Use the slider to set the strength.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_sharpen">Makes edges and details clearer. Use the slider to set the sharpness.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_vignette">Darkens the image edges and draws attention to the centre. Use the slider to set the strength.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_clarity">Emphasises textures and fine contrast. Use the slider to set the clarity.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_pixel">Pixelates the image. Use the slider to set the pixel size.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_splash">Keeps the selected colour and turns all other colours grey. Choose the colour by tapping the image or using the colour menu, then use the slider to set the tolerance.</string>
    <string name="help_content_filter_contours">Replaces black and grey drawing lines with clean black contours on a new transparent layer. Use the slider to set the contour tolerance.</string>
    <string name="place_empty_layer">The active layer has no visible content to place.</string>
